      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "The §3Lambda Launch Pad§r is a mechanism for launching the §6Lambda-98 Rocket§r, which can be used to launch satellites for cheaper and faster than the Soyuz. This launch pad works much faster than the Soyuz facility: loading the rocket and fueling takes noticeably less time, and instead of a 30 second wait after pressing the launch button, Lambda offers only 10 seconds. It also supports automatic launch after all preparation procedures are complete.\n\nThe launch pad constantly consumes §e200kHE/s§r. Each launch consumes 16000mB of §bLeaded Gasoline§r and §bHydrogen Peroxide§r. If the pad is in auto-launch mode, a countdown begins after all required slots and buffers are filled. In manual mode, the pad waits for your signal.\n\nQuest requirements: Build a §3Lambda Launch Pad§r, supply it with §e200kHE/s§r and stock §bLeaded Gasoline§r and §bHydrogen Peroxide§r. Launch a §6Lambda-98 Rocket§r. Optionally, enable auto-launch mode for automatic countdown and launch.\n\n[F1] For more information.",
